Standard scikit-learn, matplotlib, seaborn

example folder contains the pdfs and txt files generated for datasets.

Running just main.py will generate validation and learning curves for both datasets(INCLUDING GRID SEARCH!!).
    - Make sure plt_to_pdf.py is in the same directory as the .py files.
    - Running leaning curves also includes grid search. Comment the gridsearch_learning_curves() function calls to stop
    - Each .py file can also be run independently.
    - .pdf filenames are generated automatically with the current timestamp.
    - .txt files are named according to the dataset.(WILL BE OVERWRITTEN EACH TIME!!!!!)


Note: Grid search can a some time.

What each file does:
heart.py:
    -Generates parameter tuning curves for the heart dataset.
churn.py:
    -Generates parameter tuning curves for the churn dataset.
grid_heart.py:
    -Performs grid search for the heart dataset.
    -Generates learning curves for the heart dataset.
    -generates .txt file with grid search results and test set scores.
GRID_churn.py:
    -Performs grid search for the churn dataset.
    -Generates learning curves for the churn dataset.
    -generates .txt file with grid search results and test set scores.

